{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): obs are done. temperature is thirty seven point eight, pulse 92, blood pressure 132 over 78, and sats 98 percent.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): ta. the screen's just— um. sorry. what's brought you in today?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): good morning, doctor. i must apologise for coming in like this. i have a swelling in my cheek, and a throbbing toothache.",
  "[SEG0004] person_4 (CAREGIVER): it's the left side, since the—",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): sorry, say that again? the computer just beeped at me.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (PATIENT): of course. the left cheek is swollen, and there is a throb in the tooth. the dentist fitted a crown.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): a crown. and the dentist can't see you?",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (CAREGIVER): no. she's away till monday. i'm his carer. we rang the emergency line and they said come to the gp.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): mm. how long has the swelling actually been there?",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (CAREGIVER): oh. the parking. i should just—",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): one second. right. i'm logging back in.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): it has been three days, doctor. it began the evening the crown was put on.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): three days. and have you felt feverish?",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (PATIENT): a little warm since yesterday evening. i would not call it a high fever.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): is the pain there all the time, or does it ease?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): it is constant, a throb. it is worse when i lie down. i have been taking paracetemol, which dulls it for an hour or so.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): paracetamol. what dose, sorry, i missed that?",
  "[SEG0018] person_4 (CAREGIVER): he takes the two tablets, i think it's—",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): forgive me, it is one gram, four times a day. i am careful not to exceed that.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): and anything else regular? the list on here is tiny.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): ramipril, five milligrams, every morning, for my high blood pressure. that is all.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): right, high blood pressure, noted. any trouble swallowing, or with your breathing?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): no. i can swallow without difficulty, and my breathing is quite normal.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): good. and otherwise, chest, waterworks, bowels, all behaving?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): yes, doctor. all quite normal, thank you.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): let me look. left cheek is swollen and warm. tender over the upper jaw. you can only open about two fingers. no red streaking down the neck.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (CAREGIVER): it was definitely smaller yesterday. i nearly rang then but—",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): i was going to leave it at pain relief and have you wait for the dentist on monday.",
  "[SEG0029] person_4 (CAREGIVER): it's crept up towards the eye since this morning. i don't think monday is—",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): right, i didn't have that. scrap the wait-and-see. i think this is a dental infection from that crown. we'll start an antibiotic. amoxicilin— amoxicillin, five hundred milligrams, three times a day, by mouth, for five days.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): thank you. should i carry on with the paracetamol?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): yes, keep the paracetamol as you are. if you get trouble swallowing or breathing, or the swelling jumps, go straight to a and e. i'll see you back here in three days, and do try the dentist again on monday."
 ],
